    "summary": "High-energy late-'72 set with stellar Other One and tight jams",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a soaring The Other One jam, crisp leads on Playing In The Band, and a vibrant China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segue. Jerry's guitar shines throughout while the rhythm section drives strong Truckin' and Sugar Magnolia. Overall performance is high‑energy with solid song flow despite occasional mix hiccups.",
    "review": "December 10, 1972 at Winterland Arena finds the Dead in top form, launching from a frosty Cold Rain And Snow opener into a cascade of tight, inspired playing. The first set builds momentum through classics like Playing In The Band and Casey Jones, but it’s the second‑set that truly shines: an explosive Truckin' segues into a thunderous drum solo and then erupts into one of the night’s highlights—an expansive Other One where Jerry’s fluid leads soar above a buried yet still driving Phil bass line. The band locks in on China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider, delivering a bright, melodic bridge that flows seamlessly into a soulful Stella Blue before launching back into high‑octane numbers such as Sugar Magnolia and Ramble On Rose. Though the soundboard capture carries some hiss and occasional level drops—most noticeable in the bass mix—the recording captures the band’s exuberant interplay and makes this late‑'72 Winterland performance a must‑listen for fans seeking that classic, high‑energy Dead vibe.",
